# Line endings (#2180, epic #2200): text is LF in the repo and LF in every
# checkout, on every OS. Windows runners (and Git for Windows' default
# `core.autocrlf=true`) would otherwise check text out as CRLF, and fixtures
# compared byte-for-byte, snapshots, and tests that write CRLF on purpose (to
# prove the parsers handle it) would read different bytes on Windows than the
# repo holds. Minerva itself reads CRLF fine; the repo just doesn't contain any.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never converted, never diffed as text. `text=auto` detects most of
# these anyway; named so a zero-byte or ASCII-looking one can't be mistaken.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.traineddata binary
*.thumbnail binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.wasm binary
*.onnx binary
